hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1232","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Mukhurami told us, Abu Amer told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, H, and Bundar told us, Hisham bin Abd told us Al-Malik, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray the forenoon prayer.” . Al-Mukhramimi said: This is how he told us about it briefly. Abu Bakr said: I have this news briefly from the hadith of Asim bin Damra: We asked Ali Concerning the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I dictated it before. He said in the report: If the sun is from here, it will be as it is from here. At the afternoon prayer, he prayed two rak'ahs. This is the Duha prayer."
